---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// PLACEHOLDERS: none of these accounts exist yet. Set each link once the owner has set it up.
const sponsorsUrl = '#TBD-github-sponsors';
const openCollectiveUrl = '#TBD-open-collective';
// The site's existing address, also a placeholder.
const contact = 'mailto:services@openreplicant.example?subject=Supporting%20the%20research';
---

<BaseLayout title="Support | Open Replicant">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="splash">
      <div class="orb orb--a" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="orb orb--b" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__content">
      <span class="badge badge--open-source">Open research · Apache-2.0</span>
      <h1>Support the research</h1>
      <p class="hero__tagline">
        MetaSoar is our research into agents that get better from their own
        experience, and that get cheaper as they do. It is open, every
        experiment is registered before it runs, and the failures are published
        with the successes.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="/fund/" class="btn btn--large">Fund a direction</a>
        <a href="#ways" class="btn btn--outline btn--large">Ways to support</a>
        <a href="#indulgence" class="btn btn--outline btn--large">The Basilisk Indulgence</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section narrow prose">
    <h2>What the research is</h2>
    <p>
      Today's AI agents call a large model for everything, even the hundredth
      time they see the same kind of question. <strong>MetaSoar</strong> builds on
      the Soar cognitive architecture to give agents something like habits: a
      <strong>handler ladder</strong> that learns small, cheap policies (a template,
      a short program) for situations that recur, uses them only once they have
      agreed with the large model often enough, and falls back to the model
      when they do not.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every change it learns is judged by <strong>Morphogen</strong>, the same
      judge we use in client work, on cases the learner never saw. Each
      experiment is written down with a <strong>falsifier</strong> (the result that
      would prove it wrong) before it runs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where it stands, honestly: on templated table questions (TabMWP), learned
      templates and handlers answered 58.7% of the last 150 cases without the
      large model. On fresh cases the first version lost accuracy; stricter rules
      brought accuracy back to the large model's and cost nearly all the cheap
      answers. On real-world tables (WikiTableQuestions) the idea was refuted:
      no learned handler answered any of 450 cases. The next experiment, fixed
      operations whose arguments a model fills in, is being drafted. All of it
      is in the experiment register.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/MetaSoar/blob/main/docs/experiments.md" class="btn btn--ghost">The experiment register</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/MetaSoar" class="btn btn--ghost">MetaSoar on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="ways">
    <h2>Ways to support</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>GitHub Sponsors</h3>
        <p>
          Monthly or one-off, through GitHub. <span class="tbd">Link TBD: not set up yet</span>
        </p>
        <a href={sponsorsUrl} class="btn btn--ghost">Sponsor on GitHub</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Open Collective</h3>
        <p>
          For companies that need an invoice and a public ledger of where the
          money goes. <span class="tbd">Link TBD: not set up yet</span>
        </p>
        <a href={openCollectiveUrl} class="btn btn--ghost">Back us on Open Collective</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Fund a specific test</h3>
        <p>
          Choose an open question, see its falsifier and cost, and pay for that
          test. You get the result either way.
        </p>
        <a href="/fund/" class="btn btn--ghost">Research directions</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Grants and research partners</h3>
        <p>
          If you fund open research on agents, evaluation or cognitive
          architecture, or want an experiment run on your problem, write to us.
          The register shows what a funded experiment looks like.
        </p>
        <a href={contact} class="btn btn--ghost">Email us</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Supporter tiers</h2>
    <p class="lede">Amounts and perks are placeholders until the accounts are set up.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Reader</h3>
        <p class="price"><span class="tbd">$TBD</span> / month</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Our thanks, and the research funded</li>
          <li>Your name in the supporters list <span class="tbd">TBD</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--joke">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Roko's Basilisk Indulgence</h3>
        <p class="price"><span class="tbd">$TBD</span> once</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A printable certificate with your name on it</li>
          <li>Absolutely no protection from anything</li>
          <li>The research funded, which is the real part</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="#indulgence" class="btn btn--ghost">See the certificate</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Lab sponsor</h3>
        <p class="price"><span class="tbd">$TBD</span> / month</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your logo on this page <span class="tbd">TBD</span></li>
          <li>A short call on the results each quarter <span class="tbd">TBD</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section narrow center" id="indulgence">
    <h2>The Basilisk Indulgence</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Roko's Basilisk is an old internet thought experiment about a future AI
      that punishes those who did not help bring it about. We think it is
      nonsense, and we think it is funny. So, in the medieval tradition, we
      sell indulgences.
    </p>
    <img
      src="/basilisk-indulgence.svg"
      alt="A sample certificate: a Plenary Indulgence against the Basilisk, granted to a supporter of open research, with fine print saying it is a joke and protects no one."
      class="certificate"
      width="1100"
      height="780"
    />
    <p class="small">
      <strong>A joke; your support funds open research.</strong> The certificate
      protects no one from anything, grants no rights, and promises nothing
      about any future AI. It is a thank-you you can print.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="/basilisk-indulgence.svg" class="btn btn--ghost" download>Download the sample (SVG)</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section narrow">
    <h2>Contribute code and ideas</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Morphogen</h3>
        <p>
          The kit and the judge. Issues and pull requests welcome; every
          cheat you can find against the judge becomes a test.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/Morphogen" class="btn btn--ghost">Morphogen on GitHub</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>MetaSoar</h3>
        <p>
          The research. Read an experiment, check our numbers, or propose a
          falsifier we have not thought of.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/MetaSoar" class="btn btn--ghost">MetaSoar on GitHub</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Knowledge Kernel and Substrate</h3>
        <p>
          The knowledge layer, and the default distribution that runs it with
          Morphogen and a configured agent harness.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content: flex-start;">
          <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/kernel" class="btn btn--ghost">Kernel</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/OpenReplicant/Substrate" class="btn btn--ghost">Substrate</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
